1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,000
GENESIS RT: the physical world compiler for QNX

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,500
Embedded software must behave correctly
even when real systems fail.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:14,500
Describe a machine, generate native QNX software,
and prove it behaves.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:21,500
Everything starts from a machine contract:
sensors, actuators, safety limits.

5
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:28,000
The designer validates every field
before anything is built.

6
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:36,000
Genesis generates the QNX controller:
guard policy and build files.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Each file carries its source hash,
pinned against the contract.

8
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:52,000
Then it runs for real: compiled with the QNX
toolchain, executed on QNX 8 under QEMU.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,500
Sixteen checks, a thousand performance samples.
Gate: PASS.

10
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,500
Now break it: a stale-sensor fault is injected live.
The guard answers; the run records it.

11
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:11,500
A targeted verdict -- honest about
what was not re-tested.

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Diagnose with the evidence graph: every verdict
links back to scenarios, binaries, requirements.

13
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Click any node: the proof behind the claim,
ready for review.

14
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:39,000
Change one limit -- 1.2 to 1.6 meters per second --
and verify both revisions.

15
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:49,500
Before denies the 1.5 command; after allows it.
Same rigor, new behavior -- two passports.

16
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:56,500
A stale build bound to the new contract
is refused. No passport. Fail closed.

17
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:03,500
Both passports replay independently --
no servers, no trust-me step.

18
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:10,500
Before and after verify clean:
thirty-four files, fifteen links each.

19
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:18,500
Flip a single byte, and the verifier
rejects the pack. Evidence you can defend.

20
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:29,000
Specify. Compile. Run. Break. Prove.
Genesis RT for QNX.

21
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Evidence your whole team can inspect.
